<mxCell id="n1" value="&lt;b&gt;What each level returns&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:10px;color:#5B6275&quot;&gt;Population, residents due, open care gaps, gaps per 100, closure rate, coverage, residents in outreach and a breakdown by programme (care activity). The same figures drive the map, tables and Ask Anticipa.&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F1EDFF;strokeColor=#B9A8FF;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#1F2430;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="610" width="660" height="140" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="n2" value="&lt;b&gt;How it is built&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:10px;color:#5B6275&quot;&gt;GET /api/v1/analytics/geography with level country, state or district. It is served from the analytics snapshot. A district map file is applied only when reading, so resident rows are unchanged. About 20,000 residents sit in each district.&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F1EDFF;strokeColor=#B9A8FF;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#1F2430;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="720" y="610" width="680" height="140" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
